From 2a2cc2e1fd5bb995280ad9fa080d019f23674aab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler South <tsouth2@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:14:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Tell the launcher when the desktop is drawn

The launcher hides its window while Omarchy starts and shows it on a timer, which with CPU rendering showed a black window for up to 12 seconds. The agent now runs desktop-drawn for each launcher connection and says "desktop drawn" once per session. It watches Hyprland's layers over the compositor's own sockets until, on the first monitor, the shell's wallpaper layer and bar are mapped and its black startup cover is gone. The shell lifts that cover after 10 seconds even when the wallpaper is still being decoded, which on a slow PC left the desktop black for another 1 to 2 seconds, so the helper then also takes a scaled-down grim capture as the session user and looks for a wallpaper in the area the bar, dock and notifications leave free. A dark wallpaper cannot be told from an empty screen, so it reports 8 seconds after the layers anyway, and right away when the capture fails. A half second settle follows. Layer events wake it, with a one second poll as a fallback. Launchers that do not know the line ignore it.

The agent speaks version 7. Compatibility revision 72 delivers the agent and the helper to existing disks before login.
